title: Public Works
subtitle: Labour: employment, infrastructure or workers’ housing.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishProjects.cardAvailable(Q, 'public_works') !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card government.public_works (technical reference 17.11–17.12; card catalogue 8.7). Opening and closing
// the card are free; a confirmed option costs this month's action, or the one free step of an adviser
// who opened the card. Options that need a system of a later stage are shown with their reason.
PolishProjects.cardView(Q, 'public_works');
!}

= Public works

Public works belong to Labour; the Treasury alone gives no access. Each programme is large: its preparation (1 T) now, its launch (1 T) in the agenda. Working programmes add public jobs, at most 8 units in the country.

[+ pl_gc_budget +]

[+ pl_gc_projects +]

- @employment
- @infrastructure
- @housing
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@employment
title: Quick employment of the unemployed
subtitle: 2 B for 3 months, then 1 B and 2 units: 0.15 pp of output a unit and public jobs.
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.optionStatus(Q, 'public_works', 'employment').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_public_works_employment_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishProjects.chooseOption(Q, 'public_works', 'employment');
!}
go-to: result

@infrastructure
title: Transport and infrastructure
subtitle: 2 B for 4 months, then 1 B and 2 units: 0.25 pp of output a unit.
